-- title:
--   Tate dictionary for W[p] at a multiplicative prime p≥ 5
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ and $p$ a prime with $5 \le p$, and suppose $W.\Delta \ne 0$, $p \mid W.\Delta$ and $p \nmid W.c_4$; suppose further that the group of $p$-torsion points (the $p$-torsion submodule of the $\mathbb{Z}$-module of affine points of the base change of $W$ to $\operatorname{AlgebraicClosure} \mathbb{Q}$) has cardinality $p^2$. Then there exist $q_T \in \mathbb{Q}_p$, elements $\zeta, t$ of an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_p$, and an isomorphism of additive groups $\Phi \colon \mathbb{Z}/p \times \mathbb{Z}/p \to W[p](\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$, such that $q_T \ne 0$, $\|q_T\|_p = (p^{\,v_p(W.\Delta)})^{-1}$ (the valuation taken as `padicValInt`), $\zeta$ is a primitive $p$-th root of unity, $t^p$ is the image of $q_T$ under the structure map, and the following holds: for every $\mathbb{Q}_p$-automorphism $\tau$ of the algebraic closure lying in the inertia subgroup, i.e. in the image in the full automorphism group of the inertia subgroup of the decomposition subgroup of the valuation subring [`padicIntegers p`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L20), and for all natural numbers $e, c$ with $\tau\zeta = \zeta^e$ and $\tau t = \zeta^c t$, one has $(\mathrm{localGaloisToGlobal}\,p\,\tau) \cdot \Phi(i,j) = \Phi(e i + c j,\, j)$ for all $i, j \in \mathbb{Z}/p$. Here [`localGaloisToGlobal p`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L41) is the monoid homomorphism sending $\tau$ to the restriction of $\tau$, viewed $\mathbb{Q}$-semilinearly, to $\operatorname{AlgebraicClosure} \mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   This is the Tate parametrisation of the $p$-torsion of a curve with multiplicative reduction at $p$, transported to the global torsion module and expressed through the local inertia group: the line $\Phi(\,\cdot\,,0)$ is the toric line generated by the image of $\zeta$, and inertia displaces $\Phi(0,1)$, a point over $t = q_T^{1/p}$, by the Kummer character $\tau \mapsto c$ of the Tate parameter. It feeds the ramification analysis of the mod $p$ representation, being cited by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_torsion_forall_unitKummer_exists_inertia_smul_ne_of_not_dvd_padicValInt_of_five_le`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_torsion_forall_unitKummer_exists_inertia_smul_ne_of_not_dvd_padicValInt_of_five_le) and [`WeierstrassCurve.smul_inertia_displacement_eq_nsmul_of_torsion_of_dvd_discr_of_five_le`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.smul_inertia_displacement_eq_nsmul_of_torsion_of_dvd_discr_of_five_le).
